  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n1 1 1\n2 2 2\n1 1 1\nOutput:\n1\n2\n1\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n3 4 6\n3 4 6\n3 4 6\nOutput:\n3 4 6\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n2 3 3 8 1\n2 3 3 8 1\n2 3 3 8 1\nOutput:\n2 3 8 1\n\nExample 4:\n\nInput:\n2 2\n6 6\n8 8\n8 8\nOutput:\n2\n6\n8\n\nExample 5:\n\nInput:\n4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4\n2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2\n8 8 8 8\n3 3 3 3\nOutput:\n4\n2\n8\n3\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Step 1: compress each column vertically (remove consecutive equal values)\n    cols = []\n    for c in range(w):\n        col = []\n        for r in range(h):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if not col or col[-1] != val:\n                col.append(val)\n        cols.append(col)\n\n    # Step 2: deduplicate columns (keep first occurrence of each distinct column)\n    unique_cols = []\n    for col in cols:\n        if col not in unique_cols:\n            unique_cols.append(col)\n\n    # Step 3: build the output grid from the unique columns\n    max_rows = max(len(col) for col in unique_cols) if unique_cols else 0\n    out_rows = []\n    for i in range(max_rows):\n        row = [col[i] for col in unique_cols if i < len(col)]\n\n        # Step 4: compress each row horizontally (remove consecutive duplicates)\n        compressed_row = []\n        for val in row:\n            if not compressed_row or compressed_row[-1] != val:\n                compressed_row.append(val)\n        out_rows.append(compressed_row)\n\n    return out_rows\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    lines = [line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]\n    grid = [list(map(int, line.split())) for line in lines]\n    result = solve(grid)\n    for row in result:\n        print(\" \".join(map(str, row)))",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Step 1: compress each column vertically (remove consecutive equal values)\n    cols = []\n    for c in range(w):\n        col = []\n        for r in range(h):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if not col or col[-1] != val:\n                col.append(val)\n        cols.append(col)\n\n    # Step 2: deduplicate columns (keep first occurrence of each distinct column)\n    unique_cols = []\n    for col in cols:\n        if col not in unique_cols:\n            unique_cols.append(col)\n\n    # Step 3: build the output grid from the unique columns\n    max_rows = max(len(col) for col in unique_cols) if unique_cols else 0\n    out_rows = []\n    for i in range(max_rows):\n        row = [col[i] for col in unique_cols if i < len(col)]\n\n        # Step 4: compress each row horizontally (remove consecutive duplicates)\n        compressed_row = []\n        for val in row:\n            if not compressed_row or compressed_row[-1] != val:\n                compressed_row.append(val)\n        out_rows.append(compressed_row)\n\n    return out_rows\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    lines = [line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]\n    grid = [list(map(int, line.split())) for line in lines]\n    result = solve(grid)\n    for row in result:\n        print(\" \".join(map(str, row)))",
